{
  "case_id": "2023-22-1178",
  "document_hash": "3dbf852a83ba5df3ee44656fb7d1c444821eb58f143675a62264896661c581c4",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1178",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3dbf852a83ba5df3ee44656fb7d1c444821eb58f143675a62264896661c581c4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3dbf852a83ba-0000-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:47 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1178",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3dbf852a83ba5df3ee44656fb7d1c444821eb58f143675a62264896661c581c4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3dbf852a83ba-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. JOSHI: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Respondent's No Fly List claims are moot. He's not on the list. He hasn't been on the list in eight years. And he won't be put back on the list in the future based on the currently available information. That makes it absolutely clear that his return to the list for the same reasons he was put on it initially can't reasonably be expected to recur."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1178",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3dbf852a83ba5df3ee44656fb7d1c444821eb58f143675a62264896661c581c4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3dbf852a83ba-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Well, the Respondent was also concerned about the propriety of the procedures that were used to put him on the list to begin with and challenged that. So how does the declaration that you all used, how does that change the procedures that he thought were violative of his rights?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1178",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3dbf852a83ba5df3ee44656fb7d1c444821eb58f143675a62264896661c581c4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3dbf852a83ba-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Can I give you a hypothetical? He does a fundraiser for his mosque. He has no idea that the mosque is under suspicion. You put him on the No -- No Fly List. You now give him this declaration that says on the -- we're not going to put you on the No Fly List for anything that's happened in the past. Tomorrow he holds another fundraiser for the same mosque. Can you put him back on the list under this declaration?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1178",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3dbf852a83ba5df3ee44656fb7d1c444821eb58f143675a62264896661c581c4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3dbf852a83ba-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. JOSHI: No -- No Fly List determinations are not made with respect to any particular event, conduct, anything. They are always based on a totality of the information."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Joshi (Respondent counsel)",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1178",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3dbf852a83ba5df3ee44656fb7d1c444821eb58f143675a62264896661c581c4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3dbf852a83ba-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "if you accept that argument, Justice Kagan, I think you would essentially conclude that no No Fly List claim ever could be moot, and the voluntary cessation exception, the judge-made exception, to Article III would swallow the mootness rule."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1178",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3dbf852a83ba5df3ee44656fb7d1c444821eb58f143675a62264896661c581c4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3dbf852a83ba-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is the government able to say anything about how this relisting occurs or -- or, more particularly, about how often it occurs?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Joshi (Respondent counsel)",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1178",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3dbf852a83ba5df3ee44656fb7d1c444821eb58f143675a62264896661c581c4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3dbf852a83ba-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "My only point is, in the mootness context, there has been no district court that has attempted to invoke those kinds of procedures."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1178",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3dbf852a83ba5df3ee44656fb7d1c444821eb58f143675a62264896661c581c4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3dbf852a83ba-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm generally sympathetic to the idea that you don't want to disclose information, national security information, but I think you've said multiple times you already do that when the case goes to the merits in these kinds of situations. So I'm not sure that's a particular concern if you have to do it in a few more cases to establish mootness, but correct me if --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "ACLU",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1178",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3dbf852a83ba5df3ee44656fb7d1c444821eb58f143675a62264896661c581c4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3dbf852a83ba-0002-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think the ACLU's brief is probably the most comprehensive on this front, but if you look at the ACLU's brief, what they say is -- you know, sometimes, I -- I think it's about half or something like that, roughly, of these plaintiffs are removed from the No Fly List during the litigation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1178",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3dbf852a83ba5df3ee44656fb7d1c444821eb58f143675a62264896661c581c4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3dbf852a83ba-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But doesn't -- but aren't you skipping over the government's assessment of whether or not that's happening and the basis upon which the government is making that assessment?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1178",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3dbf852a83ba5df3ee44656fb7d1c444821eb58f143675a62264896661c581c4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3dbf852a83ba-0002-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mootness and standing should not be interpreted to be that different from each other because both are implementing Article III's case or controversy requirement. And that's why, as I was mentioning to Justice Kavanaugh earlier, I think, we -- we shouldn't interpret the two exceptions to -- to mootness that make it more flexible than standing unmoored from the purposes for which those exceptions were developed, which was really evasion of judicial review and, in particular, with voluntary cessation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1178",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3dbf852a83ba5df3ee44656fb7d1c444821eb58f143675a62264896661c581c4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3dbf852a83ba-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Does that mean that if you're on the No Fly List, your case is never moot if the government is unwilling to say more than it said here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1178",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3dbf852a83ba5df3ee44656fb7d1c444821eb58f143675a62264896661c581c4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3dbf852a83ba-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: You said, if it were filed today, there would be no standing. Can you explain why you think that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1178",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3dbf852a83ba5df3ee44656fb7d1c444821eb58f143675a62264896661c581c4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3dbf852a83ba-0003-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 75,
        "start": 75
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We've done -- I think, before the Ninth Circuit's decision, there was a mediation, and the mediation was in part about what is the government willing to say, and it turns out that the government is not willing to say a word more than what's in the Courtright declaration."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1178",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3dbf852a83ba5df3ee44656fb7d1c444821eb58f143675a62264896661c581c4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3dbf852a83ba-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "what could the government say in a declaration that would satisfy him?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1178",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "3dbf852a83ba5df3ee44656fb7d1c444821eb58f143675a62264896661c581c4",
